1
00:00:05,267 --> 00:00:12,167
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:38,733 --> 00:00:41,600
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:41,733 --> 00:00:43,033
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:45,133 --> 00:00:46,767
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:56,767
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:56,900 --> 00:00:59,467
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:00,633
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:00,767 --> 00:01:02,233
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,367 --> 00:01:04,033
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:07,567
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:11,700
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:13,033 --> 00:01:17,267
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:20,033
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,167 --> 00:01:22,367
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:25,267
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:28,367
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:30,367 --> 00:01:31,967
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:35,067
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:36,133
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,267 --> 00:01:37,633
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:37,767 --> 00:01:38,867
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:46,033 --> 00:01:49,233
<i> NCIA! Nobody move!</i>

24
00:01:49,367 --> 00:01:52,900
[GUNSHOTS]

25
00:01:53,033 --> 00:01:55,400
<i>- Go, go! Kill them!
- [LEVER CLICKS, POWER CUTS]</i>

26
00:01:55,533 --> 00:01:57,500
<i>Where are you?!
Show me yourself!</i>

27
00:01:57,633 --> 00:01:58,867
[GUNSHOTS]

28
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,133
- [KICK LANDS]
- [BODY THUDS]

29
00:02:00,267 --> 00:02:01,700
[POWER TURNS BACK ON]

30
00:02:01,833 --> 00:02:04,000
<i> Stop! Stop!</i>

31
00:02:04,133 --> 00:02:05,633
<i> Mr. Chan, you're under arrest.</i>

32
00:02:05,767 --> 00:02:06,900
<i>You have the right
to remain silent.</i>

33
00:02:07,033 --> 00:02:09,700
<i>You disobeyed my orders.
You broke protocol!</i>

34
00:02:09,833 --> 00:02:12,667
<i>You proved just how
stubborn you are!</i>

35
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:16,033
<i>Whatever your decision
may be, I'll accept it.</i>

36
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:18,567
<i>Punish me instead,
just spare my team.</i>

37
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:22,400
<i>Gabo's here, with the gold,
he brought it inside.</i>

38
00:02:22,533 --> 00:02:23,500
<i> He ran off with the gold?</i>

39
00:02:23,633 --> 00:02:27,400
<i>Let's wait and see.
Don't judge Gabo yet.</i>

40
00:02:31,433 --> 00:02:33,400
- [CAR HORN HONKS]
- [ENGINES REVVING]

41
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:37,200
Does it hurt here?

42
00:02:37,333 --> 00:02:38,767
- Any pain?
- No.

43
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:41,800
[BROODING MUSIC PLAYING]

44
00:02:41,933 --> 00:02:44,800
Open your mouth, please.
Stick out your tongue.

45
00:02:44,933 --> 00:02:49,967
[BROODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

46
00:02:50,133 --> 00:02:52,033
Please stand up. Help him up.

47
00:02:53,433 --> 00:02:55,000
Hey!

48
00:02:55,133 --> 00:02:56,433
Take off his clothes.

49
00:02:56,567 --> 00:03:03,100
[BROODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

50
00:03:03,233 --> 00:03:05,767
- Any pain here?
- No.

51
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:07,900
- Take off his pants.
- No!

52
00:03:08,033 --> 00:03:10,100
- What are you doing?!
- Wait.

53
00:03:10,233 --> 00:03:12,800
Mr. Chan, it's
standard procedure.

54
00:03:12,933 --> 00:03:17,000
The doctor needs to make sure
you're in good condition

55
00:03:17,133 --> 00:03:21,633
and check your existing injuries
before you go to custody.

56
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:23,933
You understand?
Go ahead, continue.

57
00:03:24,067 --> 00:03:25,567
[GRUNTS]

58
00:03:28,067 --> 00:03:30,300
[DOCTOR]
Male, conscious, and coherent.

59
00:03:30,433 --> 00:03:32,167
Vital signs, stable.

60
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:34,567
- Turn to the left, Mr. Chan.
- He has a forehead abrasion.

61
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:37,467
And... a superficial laceration
on his lip.

62
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:39,567
- Turn to the right, Mr. Chan.
- But other than that,

63
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:42,267
there are no apparent
external injuries.

64
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:43,867
Okay. Thank you, Doc.

65
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,533
Okay, turn to the front.

66
00:03:45,667 --> 00:03:52,767
- [BROODING MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

67
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:57,800
Ow, ow, ow, ow!

68
00:03:57,933 --> 00:04:00,500
Ouch!
[WHIMPERS LOUDLY]

69
00:04:00,633 --> 00:04:02,467
- I'm good.
- Sir, let's clean this up.

70
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:05,133
It's fine, we're okay.

71
00:04:05,267 --> 00:04:07,367
- Just take these.
- [GRUNTS SOFTLY]

72
00:04:08,733 --> 00:04:11,700
Can you calm down?! You
might get high blood pressure.

73
00:04:11,833 --> 00:04:14,600
If you pop a blood vessel, we'll
have to take you to the ER.

74
00:04:14,733 --> 00:04:18,533
Karen, why did you guys move
without Sir Delgado's go signal?

75
00:04:18,667 --> 00:04:21,467
For Sam.
To finally close the case.

76
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:24,467
Yeah, we followed our hearts
instead of our heads.

77
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:26,433
But we did what was right.

78
00:04:26,567 --> 00:04:28,367
Well, you're in big trouble
with Sir Delgado then.

79
00:04:28,533 --> 00:04:32,600
You could get suspended,
or worse, fired from the NCIA.

80
00:04:32,733 --> 00:04:35,933
Will you stop, Ernesto? You'd
only understand our actions

81
00:04:36,067 --> 00:04:39,067
if you had a co-agent
you truly cared about.

82
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:43,133
Excuse me, I do care
about my fellow agents.

83
00:04:44,267 --> 00:04:46,433
- You?
- Oh boy.

84
00:04:46,567 --> 00:04:47,900
Oh boy, oh boy, oh boy.

85
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:53,267
- Does it hurt?
- No, it feels good.

86
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:56,133
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING,
THEN FADES]

87
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:01,800
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

88
00:05:04,333 --> 00:05:07,700
Everything you did will
be in the report!

89
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:12,533
You guys knew this was wrong,
didn't you?!

90
00:05:14,300 --> 00:05:16,100
Didn't you?!

91
00:05:16,233 --> 00:05:18,367
Yes...

92
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:24,467
Jacinto was your team leader
on the Chinatown mission.

93
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:26,733
But didn't you know...

94
00:05:26,867 --> 00:05:29,400
Sir Delgado was taking her off

95
00:05:29,533 --> 00:05:34,000
the gold smuggling case?!

96
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:36,833
We knew that, Ma'am Pia.

97
00:05:36,967 --> 00:05:41,433
We needed to catch Mr. Chan
before he could even hide.

98
00:05:41,567 --> 00:05:42,867
[SCOFFS]

99
00:05:44,333 --> 00:05:50,300
And did you know this operation
you pulled was unofficial?

100
00:05:51,533 --> 00:05:52,533
[SEQIOA] Ma'am Pia.

101
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:55,567
We know what we are doing.

102
00:05:55,700 --> 00:05:59,000
And as a matter of fact,
we had everything under control.

103
00:05:59,567 --> 00:06:01,700
I guess you really want...

104
00:06:02,433 --> 00:06:05,200
...to ruin your careers, huh?

105
00:06:05,333 --> 00:06:07,267
With all due respect,
Ma'am Pia...

106
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,300
If you had included
in your report

107
00:06:09,467 --> 00:06:14,000
what Jacinto did in Chinatown,
this wouldn't have happened.

108
00:06:14,133 --> 00:06:16,567
So, you're blaming me?
Is that it?

109
00:06:16,700 --> 00:06:17,800
- Ma'am Pia--
- [CASTOR] Borromeo.

110
00:06:17,933 --> 00:06:19,167
Don't talk back.

111
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:23,167
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

112
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:24,400
[PIA CLICKS TEETH]

113
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:27,600
Guys, you better wake up.

114
00:06:27,733 --> 00:06:30,400
Jacinto's ship is sinking.

115
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:34,300
Don't let yourselves
drown with her.

116
00:06:38,333 --> 00:06:39,833
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

117
00:06:45,900 --> 00:06:47,867
This is what I was afraid of!

118
00:06:49,267 --> 00:06:51,100
He's alive, isn't he?

119
00:06:51,233 --> 00:06:52,833
It's nothing fatal.

120
00:06:52,967 --> 00:06:57,900
You think it's okay he got shot
just because he survived?

121
00:06:58,033 --> 00:07:00,200
Yes, he got shot.
So, what?

122
00:07:00,333 --> 00:07:03,533
I've been shot before.
So have Victor.

123
00:07:03,667 --> 00:07:05,933
This is normal
in the world we live in.

124
00:07:06,067 --> 00:07:08,367
Yes, but it could
have been avoided

125
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:10,267
if you had just listened to me!

126
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:13,033
He must experience these things.

127
00:07:13,167 --> 00:07:16,067
Iron doesn't become steel
until it has been through fire.

128
00:07:16,233 --> 00:07:17,233
Ma'am, sir.

129
00:07:20,367 --> 00:07:21,267
Doc.

130
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:23,233
How is my son?

131
00:07:23,367 --> 00:07:25,567
The bullet didn't hit
any major artery.

132
00:07:25,700 --> 00:07:27,400
He just needs rest.

133
00:07:27,533 --> 00:07:29,033
Kindly monitor him
for any infection.

134
00:07:29,167 --> 00:07:30,333
Thank you.

135
00:07:30,467 --> 00:07:31,433
You're welcome, ma'am.

136
00:07:32,933 --> 00:07:35,200
Thank you, Doc.
I'll have Arturo contact you.

137
00:07:35,333 --> 00:07:36,333
Okay.

138
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:41,267
Jacinto.

139
00:07:42,367 --> 00:07:49,267
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

140
00:07:53,167 --> 00:07:57,267
Well? Has Sir Delgado
suspended you already?

141
00:07:58,300 --> 00:08:01,200
- No.
- You sure are something.

142
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:05,233
You have the gall to risk
the lives of your comrades...

143
00:08:06,067 --> 00:08:07,900
...just to make yourself
look good.

144
00:08:08,033 --> 00:08:10,000
That isn't my intention.

145
00:08:10,133 --> 00:08:14,133
And everything I did,
I did it for the NCIA.

146
00:08:14,267 --> 00:08:15,833
Just wait for my report.

147
00:08:17,433 --> 00:08:19,500
Let's see if you can still do
anything for the agency

148
00:08:19,633 --> 00:08:20,800
after I submit it.

149
00:08:23,467 --> 00:08:25,033
You are a Jacinto.

150
00:08:25,833 --> 00:08:26,767
But...

151
00:08:28,567 --> 00:08:30,433
all you have to show for
is your name.

152
00:08:30,567 --> 00:08:36,133
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

153
00:08:36,267 --> 00:08:38,533
Hi! Is there anything I missed?

154
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,033
Yes.

155
00:08:41,833 --> 00:08:46,100
You missed the bullet
that almost killed you.

156
00:08:47,767 --> 00:08:49,633
Oh, I didn't miss it.

157
00:08:49,767 --> 00:08:52,500
I tried to dodge it,
but it grazed me.

158
00:08:52,633 --> 00:08:54,267
Still, I was marked safe.

159
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:56,367
Hmm. For now, yes.

160
00:08:57,467 --> 00:09:01,300
Let's see how long
you will be...

161
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:03,867
...safe.

162
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:09,467
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

163
00:09:17,533 --> 00:09:19,467
- [SAM SIGHS DEEPLY]
- Just ignore her.

164
00:09:20,033 --> 00:09:22,167
It's not like she hasn't
done that before.

165
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:23,800
Don't let her get to you.

166
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:29,233
- Lucas.
- Ma.

167
00:09:30,567 --> 00:09:34,067
Lucas, I trusted you,
but you failed.

168
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:38,200
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

169
00:09:38,333 --> 00:09:39,500
I'm sorry, Pa.

170
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:42,300
I'll make up for my failure.

171
00:09:42,433 --> 00:09:45,467
Mariano, let him heal first.

172
00:09:47,500 --> 00:09:48,933
I'll get back at them, Ma.

173
00:09:49,067 --> 00:09:53,700
[LUCAS BREATHING DEEPLY]

174
00:09:53,833 --> 00:09:56,433
Forget about Mr. Chan for now.

175
00:09:57,300 --> 00:09:59,133
Our men will take care of it.

176
00:10:01,667 --> 00:10:04,467
I'm not talking about Mr. Chan.

177
00:10:05,633 --> 00:10:07,200
The one who shot me!

178
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:11,833
Why? Did you see their face?

179
00:10:12,633 --> 00:10:14,600
She's from the NCIA.

180
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:17,733
The woman who arrested Victor.

181
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:20,267
- Huh?
- She's the one who shot me.

182
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,500
Samantha Jacinto.

183
00:10:24,633 --> 00:10:31,067
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

184
00:10:35,900 --> 00:10:39,267
I can't help but wonder
about the gold bars.

185
00:10:40,067 --> 00:10:41,767
Where could they be now?

186
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:48,500
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

187
00:10:48,633 --> 00:10:49,933
[BRIEFCASE CLICKS]

188
00:10:50,067 --> 00:10:51,267
[SAM] Someone else was there.

189
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:53,700
They made it easier for us
to catch Mr. Chan.

190
00:10:53,833 --> 00:10:55,433
The question is, who was it?

191
00:10:58,967 --> 00:11:00,500
Could he be the same
mysterious man

192
00:11:00,633 --> 00:11:02,867
who was the reason
we were able to arrest Tiger?

193
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:07,100
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

194
00:11:07,233 --> 00:11:13,633
[MUSIC BECOMES STIRRING]

195
00:11:35,467 --> 00:11:42,233
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

196
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:51,400
Mr. Chan.

197
00:11:52,100 --> 00:11:55,300
You are facing charges
of illegal gold mining

198
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:56,400
and money laundering.

199
00:11:56,400 --> 00:11:58,300
I don't understand Tagalog.

200
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,300
Only English.

201
00:12:00,300 --> 00:12:02,467
Okay. I'll translate it
into English for you.

202
00:12:03,700 --> 00:12:04,900
Mr. Chan.

203
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:09,733
You are under investigation
for your alleged involvement

204
00:12:09,733 --> 00:12:12,600
in illegal gold mining
and money laundering.

205
00:12:16,133 --> 00:12:17,800
You listen to me.

206
00:12:18,133 --> 00:12:19,733
I have a lot of money.

207
00:12:20,233 --> 00:12:22,667
I can give you money. Gold.

208
00:12:22,667 --> 00:12:24,300
You want gold?
I'll give you some!

209
00:12:24,667 --> 00:12:26,000
- Tell me.
- [CHUCKLES]

210
00:12:26,367 --> 00:12:27,700
How much do you want?

211
00:12:28,233 --> 00:12:29,933
Let me go. No jail.

212
00:12:30,433 --> 00:12:33,000
It looks like you want to add
to your charges, Mr. Chan.

213
00:12:33,467 --> 00:12:35,633
Bribery.
Do you want that?

214
00:12:36,433 --> 00:12:37,567
Just say it.

215
00:12:37,567 --> 00:12:38,633
No, no, no, no.

216
00:12:40,567 --> 00:12:41,700
Mr. Chan.

217
00:12:42,667 --> 00:12:43,900
I know you can understand me.

218
00:12:45,133 --> 00:12:48,633
We know that your gold came
from Victor Zafra.

219
00:12:49,067 --> 00:12:50,433
So, tell me,

220
00:12:50,433 --> 00:12:54,067
how deep is your involvement
in the syndicate?

221
00:12:57,800 --> 00:12:59,200
No more talk!

222
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:00,867
I want my lawyer!

223
00:13:01,533 --> 00:13:02,800
Do you understand?

224
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:09,333
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

225
00:13:09,333 --> 00:13:13,300
[ARTURO] Ma'am, our men saw
the NCIA arresting Mr. Chan.

226
00:13:13,300 --> 00:13:15,733
They will definitely
use Mr. Chan

227
00:13:15,733 --> 00:13:18,100
to pin this case on Victor.

228
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:20,967
We'll have a harder time
getting him out.

229
00:13:23,267 --> 00:13:25,833
It was also NCIA
who shot Lucas, right?

230
00:13:26,767 --> 00:13:30,000
[DEBORAH] The same agent
who arrested Victor.

231
00:13:31,367 --> 00:13:32,933
Samantha Jacinto.

232
00:13:35,133 --> 00:13:36,433
Well...

233
00:13:36,433 --> 00:13:39,067
your past is catching up on us.

234
00:13:39,067 --> 00:13:41,567
And our children are the ones
who have to pay for it.

235
00:13:41,567 --> 00:13:44,333
We must do something ASAP.

236
00:13:44,333 --> 00:13:51,233
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

237
00:13:53,567 --> 00:13:55,033
[BORROMEO] Ma'am Sam is here.

238
00:13:55,533 --> 00:13:56,800
- Hey, buddy.
- Sam.

239
00:14:07,100 --> 00:14:10,367
[SIGHS]

240
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:12,367
Sam?

241
00:14:13,333 --> 00:14:14,567
Are you alright?

242
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:18,900
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

243
00:14:18,900 --> 00:14:20,000
Team.

244
00:14:21,500 --> 00:14:22,767
I'm sorry

245
00:14:23,933 --> 00:14:25,400
for involving you in this.

246
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:29,533
I forced you into something
that I thought was right.

247
00:14:29,567 --> 00:14:31,300
But what I did was wrong.

248
00:14:31,667 --> 00:14:33,633
You didn't force us
into this, Sam.

249
00:14:34,667 --> 00:14:35,733
[SEQIOA] I agree with Karen.

250
00:14:36,333 --> 00:14:38,533
I mean, no need to apologize.

251
00:14:39,067 --> 00:14:41,867
The mission was still a success.

252
00:14:41,867 --> 00:14:44,933
We caught Mr. Chan, so cheer up.

253
00:14:44,933 --> 00:14:47,533
[CASTOR] And besides,
we are one team.

254
00:14:48,133 --> 00:14:49,967
We will continue to support
each other until the end.

255
00:14:51,067 --> 00:14:52,033
[ROBER] That's right.

256
00:14:52,767 --> 00:14:55,733
They'll probably understand
why we did this.

257
00:14:56,267 --> 00:14:59,733
The gold smuggling case got
stronger because of what we did.

258
00:15:00,767 --> 00:15:02,633
[BORROMEO] But, ma'am...

259
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:05,400
I hope Sir Delgado
doesn't suspend us.

260
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:08,900
Or fire us.

261
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:13,433
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

262
00:15:13,433 --> 00:15:14,567
[SEBASTIAN CHUCKLES]

263
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:19,100
You know,
you only made one mistake.

264
00:15:19,100 --> 00:15:20,267
This is based on my opinion.

265
00:15:24,433 --> 00:15:25,900
What is it?

266
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:28,300
Well, you didn't include me.

267
00:15:29,300 --> 00:15:30,533
Us.

268
00:15:30,733 --> 00:15:32,600
If we were there, they wouldn't
stand a chance against us.

269
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:33,800
Mm-hmm!

270
00:15:35,467 --> 00:15:38,367
Seb, Rallos, sorry for not
letting you in on the mission.

271
00:15:38,367 --> 00:15:39,667
Uh, Sam.

272
00:15:39,667 --> 00:15:42,800
I know that you don't trust me.

273
00:15:43,433 --> 00:15:44,700
Even if...

274
00:15:45,333 --> 00:15:47,800
I trust you with my whole life.

275
00:15:49,967 --> 00:15:51,367
Seb, it's not like that.

276
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:53,567
Things just happened
way too fast.

277
00:15:53,567 --> 00:15:55,500
Plus I thought that if there
were a lot of us,

278
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:56,767
it'd be difficult to carry
the mission out.

279
00:15:56,767 --> 00:15:58,033
I'll earn that trust.

280
00:15:58,367 --> 00:15:59,767
I deserve it, Sam.

281
00:15:59,767 --> 00:16:02,633
Some day, in every thing
that you do,

282
00:16:03,567 --> 00:16:05,367
you will come to me first.

283
00:16:06,700 --> 00:16:07,967
[SEBASTIAN CLICKS TONGUE]

284
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:15,000
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

285
00:16:22,733 --> 00:16:24,300
- [UTENSILS CLINKING]
- Mmm!

286
00:16:24,300 --> 00:16:26,100
It's delicious. It's good!

287
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:27,800
- Good meal.
- Yeah.

288
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:29,333
[DOOR SWINGS OPEN]

289
00:16:29,333 --> 00:16:30,400
[LAWIN] Pops!

290
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:33,867
Hey, Pops.

291
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:35,900
What did I tell you?

292
00:16:36,733 --> 00:16:39,500
You really can't trust Gabo.

293
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:43,800
Pops, Gabo stole all the gold

294
00:16:43,833 --> 00:16:45,333
and took them home.

295
00:16:45,333 --> 00:16:47,167
Why didn't you take
the gold back then?

296
00:16:47,167 --> 00:16:48,933
[LAWIN] Tomas, I can't take
Gabo on my own.

297
00:16:48,933 --> 00:16:51,233
Even if Uwak and I take him
on together, we won't survive.

298
00:16:52,367 --> 00:16:53,667
What are we going to do now?

299
00:16:53,667 --> 00:16:55,767
We'll just wait for Gabo.

300
00:16:55,767 --> 00:16:57,267
He'll come around soon.

301
00:16:57,267 --> 00:17:01,067
Well, we'll be waiting
for all eternity then, Pops!

302
00:17:01,067 --> 00:17:03,800
He won't come for sure.
I know how his mind works.

303
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:05,767
- He's from Ginintuang Lupa!
- Yeah!

304
00:17:05,767 --> 00:17:07,167
They're easily tempted!

305
00:17:07,167 --> 00:17:09,867
With how valuable that gold is
he's got it all to himself now!

306
00:17:12,100 --> 00:17:19,067
[ENGINE REVVING]

307
00:17:19,100 --> 00:17:26,067
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

308
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:33,600
[PAPANG] In the short time
that I've known him,

309
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:37,233
I know that he has
a kind heart.

310
00:17:37,233 --> 00:17:38,900
He will do the right thing.

311
00:17:38,900 --> 00:17:41,200
Well, let's see about that.

312
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:43,733
[DOOR CREAKS OPEN]

313
00:17:43,733 --> 00:17:47,900
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

314
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:48,900
'Tang.

315
00:17:50,300 --> 00:17:51,500
Gabo?

316
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:57,967
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

317
00:17:59,767 --> 00:18:01,100
Here's the gold.

318
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:08,133
[STIRRING MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

319
00:18:14,067 --> 00:18:17,367
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

320
00:18:17,367 --> 00:18:22,233
[SUITCASE LOCKS CLICKING]

321
00:18:25,733 --> 00:18:26,767
[OMENG] Pops.

322
00:18:27,533 --> 00:18:28,633
It's all here.

323
00:18:28,633 --> 00:18:30,600
This suitcase too, Pops.

324
00:18:40,133 --> 00:18:41,900
[PAPANG CHUCKLING]

325
00:18:46,900 --> 00:18:49,500
My judgment of your character
is correct.

326
00:18:50,767 --> 00:18:53,100
You are trustworthy.

327
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:57,567
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

328
00:18:57,567 --> 00:18:59,767
[SUITCASES CLOSING]

329
00:19:05,567 --> 00:19:07,933
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

330
00:19:07,933 --> 00:19:09,200
[DOOR OPENS, SQUEAKS]

331
00:19:11,433 --> 00:19:13,733
Sir, you didn't suspend Jacinto?

332
00:19:15,767 --> 00:19:17,500
[SCOFFING]

333
00:19:21,033 --> 00:19:23,300
Sir, you're too soft on her.

334
00:19:25,167 --> 00:19:27,133
The law is the law.

335
00:19:27,667 --> 00:19:29,367
If someone breaks it,

336
00:19:29,867 --> 00:19:31,733
they must be held accountable!

337
00:19:31,733 --> 00:19:34,100
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

338
00:19:34,100 --> 00:19:38,100
Not everything is
black and white, Pia.

339
00:19:39,900 --> 00:19:42,067
There are things that we...

340
00:19:42,833 --> 00:19:46,667
...do that are often not
in accordance with the law.

341
00:19:46,667 --> 00:19:49,533
But they're necessary.

342
00:19:49,533 --> 00:19:50,767
Necessary?

343
00:19:50,767 --> 00:19:52,300
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

344
00:19:52,300 --> 00:19:56,567
What's necessary is for you
to make a decision now.

345
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:59,833
Even at the cost
of your favorite agent.

346
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:03,100
[HUFFS]

347
00:20:03,433 --> 00:20:05,400
Just how long will you keep
taking Jacinto's side?

348
00:20:07,567 --> 00:20:09,733
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

349
00:20:09,733 --> 00:20:10,833
Remember.

350
00:20:11,167 --> 00:20:16,067
Your weakness becomes
the agency's weakness.

351
00:20:24,067 --> 00:20:26,100
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

352
00:20:26,100 --> 00:20:28,100
- [FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]
- [DOOR OPENS]

353
00:20:33,033 --> 00:20:34,067
[DOOR OPENS]

354
00:20:36,100 --> 00:20:37,100
[DOOR CLOSES]

355
00:20:38,567 --> 00:20:40,433
[KEYPAD BEEPING]

356
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:47,133
[PHONE RINGING]

357
00:20:47,600 --> 00:20:48,600
[PHONE BEEPS]

358
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:50,000
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

359
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,167
Ricardo.

360
00:20:51,167 --> 00:20:52,433
What do you need?

361
00:20:52,867 --> 00:20:56,067
We need to talk,
but not on the phone.

362
00:20:56,700 --> 00:20:58,000
Let's meet.

363
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,433
[MUSIC BECOMES SUSPENSEFUL]

364
00:20:59,433 --> 00:21:01,333
Okay. When?

365
00:21:01,967 --> 00:21:03,100
Right now.

366
00:21:07,300 --> 00:21:08,500
At this hour?

367
00:21:08,867 --> 00:21:11,033
Just send me
the meeting location.

368
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:13,200
[PHONE BEEPS]

369
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:14,267
[LINE DROPPED]

370
00:21:14,733 --> 00:21:17,767
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

371
00:21:17,767 --> 00:21:18,767
[PHONE CLATTERS]

372
00:21:22,533 --> 00:21:23,733
What's your plan?

373
00:21:24,233 --> 00:21:27,033
Talking won't work
on Ricardo anymore.

374
00:21:28,300 --> 00:21:30,433
We need to negotiate
the hard way.

375
00:21:32,933 --> 00:21:35,067
[MUSIC FADING]

376
00:21:35,467 --> 00:21:39,333
- [FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]
- [SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

377
00:21:39,333 --> 00:21:41,067
Pops, here's the money.

378
00:21:41,533 --> 00:21:42,500
[LATCHES SNAPPING OPEN]

379
00:21:54,067 --> 00:21:56,100
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

380
00:21:56,100 --> 00:21:58,467
[MONEY RUSTLING]

381
00:22:02,367 --> 00:22:03,367
Gabo.

382
00:22:10,733 --> 00:22:12,200
That's for you, Gabo.

383
00:22:12,700 --> 00:22:15,267
[GABO]
Tatang, thank you so much.

384
00:22:15,633 --> 00:22:19,133
I told you already.
Just call me Pops.

385
00:22:19,133 --> 00:22:22,467
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

386
00:22:22,467 --> 00:22:24,833
[ENVELOPE RUSTLING]

387
00:22:30,067 --> 00:22:31,467
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

388
00:22:32,467 --> 00:22:37,100
Pops, I think you gave me
too much money.

389
00:22:37,100 --> 00:22:39,833
Our deal was only 100,000 pesos.

390
00:22:39,833 --> 00:22:42,067
Well, consider it a reward
for your loyalty.

391
00:22:44,067 --> 00:22:45,067
[EXHALES SOFTLY]

392
00:22:45,067 --> 00:22:46,633
Thank you so, so much.

393
00:22:47,033 --> 00:22:48,800
I desperately need the money.

394
00:22:49,633 --> 00:22:51,800
Pops, I'll get going.

395
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:54,533
My father needs surgery now.

396
00:22:54,900 --> 00:22:56,100
Goodbye. Thanks again.

397
00:22:56,100 --> 00:22:58,433
[MUSIC FADING]

398
00:22:58,433 --> 00:23:00,233
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

399
00:23:00,233 --> 00:23:01,500
So, what now?

400
00:23:02,300 --> 00:23:03,733
Feeling embarrassed, huh?

401
00:23:03,733 --> 00:23:07,100
Because you thought Gabo
would run off with the gold.

402
00:23:07,100 --> 00:23:11,033
You assumed he would do
something bad.

403
00:23:11,033 --> 00:23:14,433
[OMENG] During our time
with Gabo behind bars,

404
00:23:14,433 --> 00:23:18,200
we witnessed
what he was really like.

405
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:19,833
He has principles.

406
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:23,233
He knows what's right and wrong.

407
00:23:23,267 --> 00:23:24,600
[LOW CHUCKLE]

408
00:23:25,367 --> 00:23:26,567
Luck!

409
00:23:27,033 --> 00:23:28,867
Just pure luck!

410
00:23:28,867 --> 00:23:32,067
Sooner or later,
his true colors will come out.

411
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:34,367
[LAWIN] That Gabo...

412
00:23:34,367 --> 00:23:36,733
If he doesn't die on a mission,

413
00:23:36,733 --> 00:23:40,733
he'll find a way to escape
and turn his back on the group.

414
00:23:41,233 --> 00:23:44,533
Just like the other released
prisoners before him.

415
00:23:44,867 --> 00:23:49,067
Gabo won't do the things
you're imagining.

416
00:23:49,067 --> 00:23:52,933
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

417
00:23:52,933 --> 00:23:54,333
- [KEYS JINGLING]
- [ENGINE TURNS ON]

418
00:23:54,333 --> 00:24:01,300
[ENGINE REVVING]

419
00:24:12,400 --> 00:24:14,300
How did you get
my number?

420
00:24:14,300 --> 00:24:16,867
[WOMAN]<i> We heard
</i> that you needed money.

421
00:24:19,200 --> 00:24:21,200
If you're going
to give us money,

422
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:23,767
then why do we have
to send you 5,000 pesos?

423
00:24:24,633 --> 00:24:26,700
[WOMAN]
<i> So I can start processing it.</i>

424
00:24:26,700 --> 00:24:28,300
<i> Just do what I said.</i>

425
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:30,433
<i> Do you want the money or not?</i>

426
00:24:30,467 --> 00:24:31,533
Nitwit!

427
00:24:31,933 --> 00:24:33,933
You're seriously
trying to scam me?

428
00:24:33,933 --> 00:24:34,933
[SCOFFS]

429
00:24:34,933 --> 00:24:36,833
We're poor,

430
00:24:36,833 --> 00:24:39,667
we're struggling
to pay hospital bills,

431
00:24:39,667 --> 00:24:42,233
and now you're trying
to scam me?!

432
00:24:42,233 --> 00:24:43,433
You can't fool me!

433
00:24:43,433 --> 00:24:44,433
You're an animal.

434
00:24:44,433 --> 00:24:46,333
May your soul burn in hell!

435
00:24:46,333 --> 00:24:47,433
You animal!

436
00:24:48,267 --> 00:24:49,433
Auntie!

437
00:24:49,433 --> 00:24:50,633
- [GABO] Hey.
- Gabo.

438
00:24:51,267 --> 00:24:52,667
- I have the money.
- [BETCHAY GASPS]

439
00:24:52,667 --> 00:24:54,333
For Papa's medicine
and his surgery.

440
00:24:54,333 --> 00:24:55,333
Thank you!

441
00:24:55,333 --> 00:24:58,033
Thank you so much
for keeping your promise!

442
00:24:58,033 --> 00:25:00,333
Gabo, where did you
get the money?

443
00:25:00,333 --> 00:25:01,567
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

444
00:25:01,600 --> 00:25:02,967
[BETCHAY] Oh, please.

445
00:25:02,967 --> 00:25:04,567
Now isn't the time for that.

446
00:25:04,567 --> 00:25:08,200
What matters is that we can
now pay for Rudy's surgery.

447
00:25:08,200 --> 00:25:09,200
Come on.

448
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:10,767
Let's go to your father.

449
00:25:10,767 --> 00:25:11,967
Let's go. Hurry.

450
00:25:13,800 --> 00:25:20,700
- [MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [MACHINE BEEPING]

451
00:25:35,767 --> 00:25:42,700
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

452
00:25:57,733 --> 00:26:04,700
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

453
00:26:20,933 --> 00:26:22,033
Gabo,

454
00:26:22,033 --> 00:26:23,500
thank you for what you did.

455
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:28,700
I won't let anything bad
happen to Papa.

456
00:26:28,700 --> 00:26:30,500
We've been separated
for so long.

457
00:26:31,633 --> 00:26:33,367
I'll do everything
to keep him alive.

458
00:26:37,333 --> 00:26:38,667
Where did you get the money?

459
00:26:40,400 --> 00:26:41,500
What was the job?

460
00:26:42,167 --> 00:26:43,667
[MAMENG] Betchay! [SNIFFLES]

461
00:26:43,667 --> 00:26:46,200
Are you going to start
an argument again?

462
00:26:53,833 --> 00:26:55,333
I found a job, that's it.

463
00:26:56,067 --> 00:26:57,100
What is it?

464
00:26:58,667 --> 00:27:00,433
What kind of job?
Is it legal?

465
00:27:02,533 --> 00:27:03,900
Someone asked me...

466
00:27:05,667 --> 00:27:07,000
to get something.

467
00:27:08,233 --> 00:27:10,033
And whatever it is,
it's none of your business.

468
00:27:10,033 --> 00:27:11,233
What thing?

469
00:27:11,233 --> 00:27:13,667
What was the thing
they asked you to get?

470
00:27:13,667 --> 00:27:14,833
What did you do?

471
00:27:14,833 --> 00:27:16,667
[MAMENG SOBBING] Betchay!

472
00:27:16,700 --> 00:27:18,533
That's enough.

473
00:27:18,533 --> 00:27:21,533
What matters is we got
the money because of Gabo.

474
00:27:21,533 --> 00:27:24,267
We were able to pay
for Rudy's surgery.

475
00:27:25,233 --> 00:27:26,767
[BETCHAY SIGHS EXASPERATEDLY]

476
00:27:28,133 --> 00:27:29,267
Pops.

477
00:27:29,833 --> 00:27:32,767
You seem happy with
how Gabo's mission turned out.

478
00:27:33,600 --> 00:27:35,000
Tomas,

479
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:38,867
Gabo just proved
that Pops can trust him.

480
00:27:40,133 --> 00:27:42,100
He didn't deny

481
00:27:42,100 --> 00:27:44,733
that for a moment he was tempted
to run away with the gold.

482
00:27:44,733 --> 00:27:46,800
In a moment of temptation,

483
00:27:46,800 --> 00:27:51,500
a person's true character
and principles show.

484
00:27:53,500 --> 00:27:54,600
[DOOR OPENS]

485
00:27:57,067 --> 00:27:59,133
Are you Rudy Magtibay's family?

486
00:27:59,133 --> 00:28:00,400
Yes, that's us.

487
00:28:01,467 --> 00:28:02,733
How's my father?

488
00:28:02,733 --> 00:28:05,133
- The surgery was successful.
- [BETCHAY CRIES]

489
00:28:05,133 --> 00:28:07,467
[SURGEON] Let's just wait
for him to wake up.

490
00:28:07,467 --> 00:28:09,467
[BETCHAY CRYING]

491
00:28:09,467 --> 00:28:10,833
Thank you so, so much, Doc.

492
00:28:10,833 --> 00:28:12,067
Thank you.

493
00:28:12,067 --> 00:28:15,400
[BETCHAY, MAMENG CRYING]

494
00:28:15,400 --> 00:28:16,500
[MAMENG] Thank you.

495
00:28:16,500 --> 00:28:23,467
[ROUSING MUSIC PLAYING]

496
00:28:24,533 --> 00:28:25,967
[PAPANG] Gabo is ready.

497
00:28:27,633 --> 00:28:31,633
If there's anyone who has
to face a bigger decision,

498
00:28:31,633 --> 00:28:32,800
it's Gabo.

499
00:28:36,533 --> 00:28:38,800
- Let's drink to that.
- [GLASSES CLINK]

500
00:28:48,533 --> 00:28:55,567
[ROUSING MUSIC CONTINUES]

501
00:29:02,333 --> 00:29:04,500
<i>Whether they're
businessmen, politicians,</i>

502
00:29:04,500 --> 00:29:06,700
<i>or treasure hunters that
secretly dig up the ground</i>

503
00:29:06,700 --> 00:29:08,533
<i> in different parts
of provinces,</i>

504
00:29:08,533 --> 00:29:10,433
<i> and when they return,</i>

505
00:29:10,433 --> 00:29:12,333
<i> they suddenly became rich.</i>

506
00:29:12,333 --> 00:29:13,867
<i> From what I've heard, sir,</i>

507
00:29:13,867 --> 00:29:15,467
<i> it's tons and tons of gold.</i>

508
00:29:15,467 --> 00:29:17,133
<i>- What is that?
- A treasure map.</i>

509
00:29:18,033 --> 00:29:19,433
<i> I feel bad for you, Gabo.</i>

510
00:29:19,433 --> 00:29:21,667
<i>You shouldn't have
to live like this.</i>

511
00:29:21,667 --> 00:29:23,633
Remember when you were a child?

512
00:29:23,633 --> 00:29:24,733
<i> I do, Pa.</i>

513
00:29:24,733 --> 00:29:26,533
- [KID CRYING]
<i> - Gabriel, listen to me.</i>

514
00:29:26,533 --> 00:29:28,200
- [GUNSHOT]
<i> - Listen to Mommy, okay?</i>

515
00:29:28,200 --> 00:29:29,967
<i> I remember everything.</i>

516
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:32,400
<i> This job Umali asked us to do,</i>

517
00:29:32,400 --> 00:29:36,167
<i> if we fail,
it'll be a big loss for us.</i>

518
00:29:36,167 --> 00:29:37,533
<i> I won't fight back, boss!</i>

519
00:29:37,533 --> 00:29:39,600
<i>It's not the reporter
who caught us.</i>

520
00:29:39,600 --> 00:29:40,600
<i>- Who is it?
- [BLOWS LAND]</i>

521
00:29:40,600 --> 00:29:41,733
<i> We don't know him.</i>

522
00:29:41,733 --> 00:29:42,833
<i> How many were they?</i>

523
00:29:42,833 --> 00:29:44,167
<i> He's alone.</i>

524
00:29:44,167 --> 00:29:46,900
<i>I'm asking you
so answer me properly!</i>

525
00:29:46,900 --> 00:29:50,667
<i>The admin put you on
preventive suspension.</i>

526
00:29:50,667 --> 00:29:52,533
<i>The next time you do
something to tarnish my name,</i>

527
00:29:52,533 --> 00:29:53,633
<i>I won't kick you
out of the house,</i>

528
00:29:53,633 --> 00:29:55,467
<i> I'll disown you.</i>

529
00:29:55,467 --> 00:29:56,467
<i> Rudy!</i>

530
00:29:56,467 --> 00:29:57,667
<i> Show yourself!</i>

531
00:29:57,667 --> 00:29:59,733
<i> I need to find that cop.</i>

532
00:29:59,733 --> 00:30:01,000
<i> Mommy loves you so much.</i>

533
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:03,133
<i> He needs to pay
for what he did to my mother.</i>

534
00:30:03,167 --> 00:30:05,033
<i> - Get out of here, hurry!
</i>- [GUNSHOTS]

535
00:30:05,033 --> 00:30:07,433
<i> Have mercy on my family!
Just take me!</i>

536
00:30:07,433 --> 00:30:08,800
<i> You animal!</i>

537
00:30:08,800 --> 00:30:10,433
<i> And for what he did to you.</i>

538
00:30:10,433 --> 00:30:14,467
<i>You really chose
that filthy Rudy!</i>

539
00:30:14,467 --> 00:30:16,867
<i> Please don't hurt my son
and my husband!</i>

540
00:30:16,867 --> 00:30:18,233
- [GUNSHOT]
<i> - Find out</i>

541
00:30:18,233 --> 00:30:19,967
<i>where more of the gold
is hidden.</i>

542
00:30:19,967 --> 00:30:22,333
<i> He's the reason
why we're struggling.</i>

543
00:30:22,333 --> 00:30:23,800
<i> I need to find him!</i>

544
00:30:23,800 --> 00:30:24,900
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVS]

545
00:30:24,900 --> 00:30:25,833
[BODY THUDS]
